  ('lemurian-shark-tooth-serpent-slayer-battle-axe-large', 'Shark Tooth "Serpent Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Battle-Axe (Large)', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '3D6 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Serrated battle-axe (large) edged with one or two rows of shark teeth, for clubbing, chopping and slashing; it also saws wood and fells trees. Damage is doubled against dragons, sea serpents, sea monsters, demons of aquatic or reptilian kind and the Splugorth''s Metztla. Thrown as far as an ordinary weapon of its type. 300-600 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-shark-tooth-serpent-slayer-dagger-or-hand-axe', 'Shark Tooth "Serpent Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Dagger or Hand Axe', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '1D6 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Serrated dagger or hand axe edged with one or two rows of shark teeth, for clubbing, chopping and slashing; it also saws wood and fells trees. Damage is doubled against dragons, sea serpents, sea monsters, demons of aquatic or reptilian kind and the Splugorth''s Metztla. Thrown as far as an ordinary weapon of its type. 300-600 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-shark-tooth-serpent-slayer-short-sword', 'Shark Tooth "Serpent Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Short Sword', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '1D6+1 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Serrated short sword edged with one or two rows of shark teeth, for clubbing, chopping and slashing; it also saws wood and fells trees. Damage is doubled against dragons, sea serpents, sea monsters, demons of aquatic or reptilian kind and the Splugorth''s Metztla. Thrown as far as an ordinary weapon of its type. 300-600 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-shark-tooth-serpent-slayer-large-sword', 'Shark Tooth "Serpent Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Large Sword', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '2D6+2 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Serrated large sword edged with one or two rows of shark teeth, for clubbing, chopping and slashing; it also saws wood and fells trees. Damage is doubled against dragons, sea serpents, sea monsters, demons of aquatic or reptilian kind and the Splugorth''s Metztla. Thrown as far as an ordinary weapon of its type. 300-600 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-shark-tooth-serpent-slayer-spear', 'Shark Tooth "Serpent Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Spear', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '2D4 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Serrated spear edged with one or two rows of shark teeth, for clubbing, chopping and slashing; it also saws wood and fells trees. Damage is doubled against dragons, sea serpents, sea monsters, demons of aquatic or reptilian kind and the Splugorth''s Metztla. Thrown as far as an ordinary weapon of its type. 300-600 P.P.E. to create. As a long weapon it may be of the collapsible kind, folding to one-third length (about 2 ft/0.6 m) for carrying. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-shark-tooth-serpent-slayer-trident', 'Shark Tooth "Serpent Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Trident', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '3D6+3 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Serrated trident edged with one or two rows of shark teeth, for clubbing, chopping and slashing; it also saws wood and fells trees. Damage is doubled against dragons, sea serpents, sea monsters, demons of aquatic or reptilian kind and the Splugorth''s Metztla. Thrown as far as an ordinary weapon of its type. 300-600 P.P.E. to create. As a long weapon it may be of the collapsible kind, folding to one-third length (about 2 ft/0.6 m) for carrying. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-shark-tooth-serpent-slayer-war-club', 'Shark Tooth "Serpent Slayer" Bio-Weapon: War Club', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '3D4+2 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Serrated war club edged with one or two rows of shark teeth, for clubbing, chopping and slashing; it also saws wood and fells trees. Damage is doubled against dragons, sea serpents, sea monsters, demons of aquatic or reptilian kind and the Splugorth''s Metztla. Thrown as far as an ordinary weapon of its type. 300-600 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-wood-undead-slayer-cane-or-walking-stick', 'Wood "Undead Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Cane or Walking Stick', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '1D6 S.D.C., or 1D6 M.D. with the aura activated', 1, NULL, 'Bio-Energy aura: 4 activations per 24 hours, 5 minutes (20 melee rounds) each; then recharge one hour at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 30 P.P.E. from a mage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wooden cane or walking stick drawn out of a single living tree. It does S.D.C. damage until its Bio-Energy aura is switched on (one melee action of concentration), then M.D. for five minutes; four activations a day, and anyone can use it while charged. Vampires and others vulnerable to wood take double damage even with no aura. On a ley line the aura is doubled, tripled at a nexus. 280-460 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-wood-undead-slayer-dagger-or-stake', 'Wood "Undead Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Dagger or Stake', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '1D6 S.D.C., or 1D6 M.D. with the aura activated', 1, NULL, 'Bio-Energy aura: 4 activations per 24 hours, 5 minutes (20 melee rounds) each; then recharge one hour at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 30 P.P.E. from a mage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wooden dagger or stake drawn out of a single living tree. It does S.D.C. damage until its Bio-Energy aura is switched on (one melee action of concentration), then M.D. for five minutes; four activations a day, and anyone can use it while charged. Vampires and others vulnerable to wood take double damage even with no aura. On a ley line the aura is doubled, tripled at a nexus. 280-460 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-wood-undead-slayer-javelin', 'Wood "Undead Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Javelin', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '2D4 S.D.C., or 2D4 M.D. with the aura activated', 1, NULL, 'Bio-Energy aura: 4 activations per 24 hours, 5 minutes (20 melee rounds) each; then recharge one hour at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 30 P.P.E. from a mage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wooden javelin drawn out of a single living tree. It does S.D.C. damage until its Bio-Energy aura is switched on (one melee action of concentration), then M.D. for five minutes; four activations a day, and anyone can use it while charged. Vampires and others vulnerable to wood take double damage even with no aura. On a ley line the aura is doubled, tripled at a nexus. 280-460 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132', NULL),
  ('lemurian-wood-undead-slayer-spear', 'Wood "Undead Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Spear', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '2D6 S.D.C., or 2D6 M.D. with the aura activated', 1, NULL, 'Bio-Energy aura: 4 activations per 24 hours, 5 minutes (20 melee rounds) each; then recharge one hour at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 30 P.P.E. from a mage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wooden spear drawn out of a single living tree. One piece of wood with either a sharpened point or a flat, arrow-like head. As a long weapon it may be of the collapsible kind, folding to one-third length (about 2 ft/0.6 m) for carrying. It does S.D.C. damage until its Bio-Energy aura is switched on (one melee action of concentration), then M.D. for five minutes; four activations a day, and anyone can use it while charged. Vampires and others vulnerable to wood take double damage even with no aura. On a ley line the aura is doubled, tripled at a nexus. 280-460 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132-133', NULL),
  ('lemurian-wood-undead-slayer-staff', 'Wood "Undead Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Staff', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '2D6 S.D.C., or 2D6 M.D. with the aura activated', 1, NULL, 'Bio-Energy aura: 4 activations per 24 hours, 5 minutes (20 melee rounds) each; then recharge one hour at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 30 P.P.E. from a mage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wooden staff drawn out of a single living tree. As a long weapon it may be of the collapsible kind, folding to one-third length (about 2 ft/0.6 m) for carrying. It does S.D.C. damage until its Bio-Energy aura is switched on (one melee action of concentration), then M.D. for five minutes; four activations a day, and anyone can use it while charged. Vampires and others vulnerable to wood take double damage even with no aura. On a ley line the aura is doubled, tripled at a nexus. 280-460 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132-133', NULL);

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO gear (slug, name, system, category, weight_lbs, cost, cost_note, damage, is_mega_damage, range, payload, rate_of_fire, ar, sdc, mdc, description, source_book, vehicle_slug) VALUES
  ('lemurian-wood-undead-slayer-short-sword', 'Wood "Undead Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Short Sword', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '1D6+2 S.D.C., or 1D6+2 M.D. with the aura activated', 1, NULL, 'Bio-Energy aura: 4 activations per 24 hours, 5 minutes (20 melee rounds) each; then recharge one hour at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 30 P.P.E. from a mage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wooden short sword drawn out of a single living tree. The only sword form made. It does S.D.C. damage until its Bio-Energy aura is switched on (one melee action of concentration), then M.D. for five minutes; four activations a day, and anyone can use it while charged. Vampires and others vulnerable to wood take double damage even with no aura. On a ley line the aura is doubled, tripled at a nexus. 280-460 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132-133', NULL),
  ('lemurian-wood-undead-slayer-throwing-stick', 'Wood "Undead Slayer" Bio-Weapon: Throwing Stick', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '2D4 S.D.C., or 2D4 M.D. with the aura activated', 1, '80 feet (24.4 m) thrown', 'Bio-Energy aura: 4 activations per 24 hours, 5 minutes (20 melee rounds) each; then recharge one hour at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 30 P.P.E. from a mage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wooden throwing stick drawn out of a single living tree. It does S.D.C. damage until its Bio-Energy aura is switched on (one melee action of concentration), then M.D. for five minutes; four activations a day, and anyone can use it while charged. Vampires and others vulnerable to wood take double damage even with no aura. On a ley line the aura is doubled, tripled at a nexus. 280-460 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132-133', NULL),
  ('lemurian-wood-undead-slayer-war-club', 'Wood "Undead Slayer" Bio-Weapon: War Club', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '2D6 S.D.C., or 2D6 M.D. with the aura activated', 1, NULL, 'Bio-Energy aura: 4 activations per 24 hours, 5 minutes (20 melee rounds) each; then recharge one hour at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 30 P.P.E. from a mage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wooden war club drawn out of a single living tree. It does S.D.C. damage until its Bio-Energy aura is switched on (one melee action of concentration), then M.D. for five minutes; four activations a day, and anyone can use it while charged. Vampires and others vulnerable to wood take double damage even with no aura. On a ley line the aura is doubled, tripled at a nexus. 280-460 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.132-133', NULL),
  ('lemurian-serpent-bio-weapon-serpent-blade', 'Serpent Bio-Weapon: Serpent Blade', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '2D6 M.D. blade; 4D6 M.D. when hot with Bio-Energy; heat blast 3D6 M.D.', 1, 'Melee; heat blast 100 feet (30.5 m)', 'Aura: 4 activations per 24 hours, 5 minutes (20 melee rounds) each; then recharge two hours at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 45 P.P.E. from a mage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Curved blade, serrated on the inside. Unpowered it cuts for 2D6 M.D.; activated (one melee action of concentration) it glows red hot for five minutes and hits for 4D6 M.D., and can throw 3D6 M.D. heat blasts to 100 feet. Double damage to anything vulnerable to fire or Bio-Energy, such as undead. Four activations a day; anyone can use it while charged. 750 P.P.E. to create. Made from the biomass of a Serpent Hunter''s Thrall Sea Serpent; reserved for Serpent Hunters and now and then awarded to an Oceanic Guardsman, Birdman or hero of Lemuria (rarely an outsider). As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.133', NULL),
  ('lemurian-serpent-bio-weapon-serpent-trident', 'Serpent Bio-Weapon: Serpent Trident', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '5D6 M.D. at full length (1D6x10 M.D. to dragons, sea serpents, giant snakes and reptilian demons and monsters); 3D6 M.D. shortened; electrical bolt 4D6 M.D.', 1, '500 feet (152 m) thrown; electric bolt 2,000 feet (610 m)', '20 electric bolts; recharge three hours at a ley line, nexus or stone pyramid, or 70 P.P.E. from a mage.', 'Each blast counts as one melee attack.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Lance-like spear with three blades, the middle one longest; the Serpent Hunters'' main weapon. It shrinks to one-fifth length (2 ft/0.6 m), where it is used like a short sword for 3D6 M.D.; at full length 5D6 M.D., more on a mounted charge (see Serpent Riding). Fires 20 electric bolts per charge; anyone can use it while charged. On a ley line bolt damage and payload are doubled, tripled at a nexus. 950 P.P.E. to create. Made from the biomass of a Serpent Hunter''s Thrall Sea Serpent; reserved for Serpent Hunters and now and then awarded to an Oceanic Guardsman, Birdman or hero of Lemuria (rarely an outsider). As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.133', NULL),
  ('lemurian-crab-claw-gauntlet', 'Crab Claw Gauntlet', 'rifts', 'weapon', 40, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', 'Stab or slash 3D6 M.D.; scissor cut 5D6 M.D. (counts as two melee attacks); blunt strike 2D4 M.D.', 1, 'Close combat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Living glove with two pincer blades, sharp on both edges, that open and shut on mental command. +2 to parry and disarm; it can parry bullets and energy blasts at -6. Each gauntlet has 3D6+50 M.D.C., harmed only when deliberately targeted, and regenerates 2D6 M.D.C. per hour; losing one pincer blade halves damage and ends scissor cuts. Also used to cut hulls, hatches, rigging, wreckage and scrap. Usually carried by designated warriors and specialists. 450 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks and needs no host. Its powers are triggered mentally through Telepathy, Empathic Connection with Animals or a Biomancer''s Communicate with Plants and Animals; P.P.E. held in it cannot be drawn on for spells.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.133-134', NULL),
  ('lemurian-serpent-entangler-net', 'Serpent Entangler Net', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', 'None', 0, '200 feet (61 m) thrown', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Net tipped with bolas, for taking sea serpents, dragon hatchlings and other targets alive. +2 to entangle; works equally well above and below water, and flies back to be thrown again after a miss. The net has 3D4x10 M.D.C. if itself targeted. Cutting a hole to free one victim takes 3D6+10 M.D. (rolled per person or creature caught), but the net regrows 2D6 M.D.C. every melee round, and a victim who is not out in time is trapped again. 400 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian Bio-Weapon it needs no host.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.134', NULL),
  ('lemurian-tentacle-sword', 'Tentacle Sword', 'rifts', 'weapon', 4.5, NULL, 'Never sold by Lemurians; all Bio-Weapons are valued as magic weapons at 50,000-200,000 credits depending on the weapon, its damage and special abilities (general figure, printed 131).', '2D6+1 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Sword-breaker built to fight other swordsmen. The central blade thrusts and parries normally while two side tentacles seize and tangle the opposing weapon, and a small tentacle at the hilt wraps the wielder''s hand. +3 to disarm, +4 to entangle, and opponents are -3 to disarm the wielder. 150 P.P.E. to create. As a Lemurian melee Bio-Weapon it can hurt beings harmed only by special attacks (vampires, werebeasts and the like), has 1D6x10+20 M.D.C. of its own if targeted, regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per minute, and needs no host.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.134', NULL),
  ('lemurian-bio-energy-bow', 'Lemurian Bio-Energy Bow', 'rifts', 'weapon', 4, 35000, '35,000-70,000 credits on the open market.', '3D6 M.D.; double damage to vampires, the undead, Metztla and Alien Intelligences', 1, '1,200 feet (366 m); half underwater', '40 energy bolts; recharge two hours at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus, or 35 P.P.E. from any wizard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Stringless bow grown from a living tree or coral. The archer arms it with a mental command (Telepathy, Communicate with Plants and Animals, or Empathic Connection with Animals) and mimes drawing a string; letting go looses a bolt of Bio-Energy. Range is halved underwater. Holds 40 bolts, then needs two hours at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus or 35 P.P.E. from any wizard. 200 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.134', NULL),
  ('lemurian-clamshell-pistol', 'Clamshell Pistol', 'rifts', 'weapon', 0.75, 7000, '7,000-15,000 credits on the open market.', '2D4 M.D.', 1, '500 feet (152 m); half underwater', '15 shots; recharge one hour at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus, or 20 P.P.E. from any wizard.', 'Each shot counts as one melee attack.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Tiny magical handgun that shoots stinging pearl pellets; the grip folds away to make it smaller still. A common backup arm of Sea Sentinels, submarine crews and scouts. Range is halved underwater. Holds 15 shots, then needs one hour at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus or 20 P.P.E. from any wizard. 100 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.134', NULL),
  ('lemurian-ink-gun', 'Ink Gun', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2, 5000, '5,000-7,000 credits on the open market.', 'None', 0, '2,000 feet (610 m)', '12 ink charges; recharge two hours at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus, or 20 P.P.E., or load spare ink packs.', 'Each blast counts as one melee attack/action.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Underwater flare gun and smoke launcher. It fires a charged ink ball that bursts at the chosen distance into an opaque cloud about 40 feet (12.2 m) across: black or blue for cover, bright colours to mark a target or signal. Often issued to Sea Sentinels and Lemurian Scouts. Holds 12 charges, restored by two hours at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus, 20 P.P.E. from any practitioner of magic, or spare ink packs. 80 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.135', NULL),
  ('lemurian-lava-projector', 'Lava Projector', 'rifts', 'weapon', 6, 35000, '35,000-60,000 credits on the open market.', 'Area-effect mode 2D6 M.D. to everything in a 10 foot (3 m) radius; stream mode 4D6 M.D. to one target', 1, '50 feet (15 m) area-effect mode, 600 feet (183 m) stream mode; half underwater', '12 blasts/uses; recharge at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus, or 35 P.P.E. from any practitioner of magic.', 'Each blast or use counts as one melee attack.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Stone Magic staff or rod that throws molten rock, either showered over an area or as an aimed stream. The lava can also be cooled and used to plug gaps in hulls or undersea walls; sealing one crack is one use. Range is halved underwater. Holds 12 blasts or uses, restored at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus (no time given) or by 35 P.P.E. from any practitioner of magic. 190 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.135', NULL),
  ('lemurian-nematocyst-paralyzer', 'Nematocyst Paralyzer', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2, 30000, '30,000-60,000 credits on the open market.', '1D4 S.D.C. to S.D.C. creatures, one M.D. to Mega-Damage creatures, plus stun', 0, '100 feet (30.5 m)', 'Six shots; recharge two hours at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus, or 40 P.P.E. from a practitioner of magic.', 'One shot per melee attack/action of the user.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Glassy rod made with a school of jellyfish; used as a club or fired like a spear gun, it delivers a paralysing toxin. Save vs non-lethal poison (16+) or be stunned for 1D4+2 melee rounds: initiative lost, attacks cut to two per melee, -8 to Perception, to strike and to all other combat bonuses, skills at -50%, Spd down 75%. Mega-Damage creatures take half the penalties for half as long. Useless through body armor and against robots and bionics. Proficiency needs W.P. Harpoon & Spear Gun. 145 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.135', NULL),
  ('lemurian-sea-urchin-spike-launcher-spear-gun', 'Sea Urchin Spike Launcher/Spear Gun', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3.5, 20000, '20,000-40,000 credits on the open market.', '1D6 M.D. per spike, 3D6 M.D. for a burst of four; 2D6 M.D. as a club', 1, '800 feet (244 m), 500 feet (152 m) underwater', '30 P.P.E. provides 12 shots.', 'Each shot or burst counts as one melee attack/action.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Black, chitin-like rod made with a group of sea urchins. It shoots 6 inch (0.15 m) spikes singly or in four-spike bursts (bursts get only half the usual strike bonuses), and the spines on its top edge let it be swung as a club for 2D6 M.D. Proficiency needs W.P. Harpoon & Spear Gun. 200 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.135', NULL),
  ('lemurian-sonic-blast-staff', 'Sonic Blast Staff', 'rifts', 'weapon', 5.5, 15000, '15,000-25,000 credits on the open market.', '3D6 S.D.C. to everything within 50 feet (15 m)', 0, '50 foot (15 m) diameter of effect', '8 uses; recharge on a ley line or nexus, or 20 P.P.E. from any mage.', 'Each use counts as one melee attack/action.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Staff that lets out a sonic shriek hitting friend and foe alike within 50 feet; only the user is immune. Sea creatures and anyone without sound protection, Mega-Damage beings included, are -4 on initiative, -1 to strike and -2 to both parry and dodge for three melee rounds; the penalties do not stack. Normally issued to Bio-Armored troops or mages who can shield themselves. Eight uses, restored on a ley line or nexus (no time given) or by 20 P.P.E. from any mage. 100 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.136', NULL),
  ('lemurian-stonecaster-pistol', 'Stonecaster Pistol', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2.2, 45000, '45,000-90,000 credits on the open market.', 'Sedimentary 1D6 M.D. to a 10 foot (3 m) diameter; Igneous 2D4 M.D. on impact and 1D4 M.D. for the next two melee rounds; Metamorphic 4D4 M.D.', 1, '1,000 feet (305 m)', '12 rounds; recharge two hours at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus, or 25 P.P.E. from any mage; or load a clip of blank stone projectiles.', 'Each shot counts as one melee attack/action.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Stone Magic sidearm of Oceanic Guardsmen and Serpent Hunters, made as a pistol or as a rod or scepter. The user picks the round: sedimentary shatters over a small area, igneous clings and keeps burning, metamorphic is dense and armor-piercing. In Lemuria Stonecasters go only to the military caste. Twelve rounds; blank stone clips can be loaded and then enchanted into any round type. 150 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.136', NULL),
  ('lemurian-stonecaster-rifle', 'Stonecaster Rifle', 'rifts', 'weapon', 7.2, 80000, '80,000-150,000 credits on the open market.', 'Sedimentary 2D6 M.D. to a 12 foot (3.6 m) diameter; Igneous 3D6 M.D. on impact and 1D6 M.D. for each of the next two melee rounds; Metamorphic 5D6 M.D.', 1, '2,000 feet (610 m); half underwater', '20 rounds; recharge four hours at a ley line, stone pyramid or nexus, or 60 P.P.E. from any mage; or load a clip of neutral stone projectiles.', 'Each shot counts as one melee attack/action.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Long-range big brother of the Stonecaster Pistol, with the same three Stone Magic rounds: sedimentary shatters over an area, igneous clings and keeps burning, metamorphic is dense and armor-piercing. Range is halved underwater. Highly prized; in Lemuria Stonecasters go only to the military caste. Twenty rounds; clips of neutral stone can be loaded and then enchanted into any round type. 300 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.136', NULL),
  ('lemurian-waterjet-gun', 'Waterjet Gun', 'rifts', 'weapon', 4.5, 30000, '30,000-60,000 credits on the open market.', '2D6 S.D.C. underwater, 4D6 S.D.C. on land; vampires take 6D6+6 to Hit Points', 0, '800 feet (244 m)', 'Effectively unlimited underwater, 20 blasts on land; refills in 10 minutes immersed in water, or 1D4 blasts per hour from moist air.', 'Each blast counts as one melee attack/action.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Rod or staff, sometimes built like a submachine-gun, that shoots a tight jet of water: S.D.C. damage to ordinary targets and direct Hit Point damage to vampires. Unlimited shots underwater, 20 on land. It refills itself in 10 minutes when dipped in any water, or pulls moisture from the air for 1D4 blasts per hour (+2 in jungle, forest or humid air, half in desert). 194 P.P.E. to create.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.136', NULL),
  ('lemurian-morphic-riding-bio-construct-living-saddle', 'Morphic Riding Bio-Construct (Living Saddle)', 'rifts', 'gear', 90, 15000, '15,000-30,000 credits on the open market (a third of that in Lemuria). Creation Cost: 175 P.P.E.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A living symbiote saddle with 1D4x10+40 M.D.C. of its own, grown by a ritual only high level Biomancer Gene-Mages know. Tendrils anchor it to the mount and it reshapes to fit any animal. It can grow extra seats for as many passengers as the mount can carry: usually one more on a horse-sized animal, 4-8 on a dragon or sea serpent. The tendrils also lash down cargo so the mount can haul its full capacity in comfort, shifting the load when it senses soreness. Unused, it shrinks to a small patch on the animal''s back or can be taken off, but it must spend at least 2D6+8 hours a week on a host animal to stay alive.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.136-137', NULL),
  ('lemurian-morphic-riding-bio-barding', 'Morphic Riding Bio-Barding', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 150000, 'Adds 150,000-300,000 credits to the cost of the animal. Creation Cost: 820 P.P.E.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Living armor grown from the riding animal itself and permanently part of it, with a built-in saddle that appears when wanted. The animal''s M.D.C. rises 50% over most of its body and is doubled for the underbelly, neck and head. Its weight goes up 20% and its Spd and leaping distance drop 10%. Whatever natural immunities or resistances the animal has (fire, cold and so on) cover the barding too. Damaged plates flake away and regrow: 2D6 M.D.C. per hour, twice that on a ley line or at a stone pyramid, three times at a nexus. The saddle seats one rider and one passenger (two passengers on a large animal) and holds only about half the mount''s usual gear.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.137', NULL),
  ('lemurian-bio-skin-gill-suit', 'Bio-Skin Gill Suit', 'rifts', 'armor', NULL, 25000, '25,000-40,000 credits on the open market; 5% of that to Lemurians in Lemuria; seldom sold to outsiders. Creation Cost: 82 P.P.E.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A medium green symbiotic second skin, usually given to surface dwellers. Main body 2D6+22 M.D.C., regrowing 1D4 M.D.C. per hour. The wearer breathes underwater like a gilled creature with no time limit, stays dry and comfortable, is shielded from cold and can survive down to two miles (3.2 km). Like every Bio-Skin it looks like anchored seaweed until invited to join a wearer by Telepathy or Empathic Connection with Animals, works on instinct for as long as it is worn, and lives on ambient P.P.E. and filter-fed plankton, algae and bacteria. Most non-Lemurian buyers cannot care for it and it dies in 2D4+1 days.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.137', NULL),
  ('lemurian-bio-skin-dive-suit', 'Bio-Skin Dive Suit', 'rifts', 'armor', NULL, 35000, '35,000-60,000 credits on the open market; 5% of that to Lemurians in Lemuria; seldom sold to outsiders. Creation Cost: 98 P.P.E.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A Caribbean blue symbiotic second skin for deep sea exploration and salvage, worn by Lemurians and their allies. Main body 2D6+33 M.D.C., regrowing 1D6 M.D.C. per hour. The wearer breathes underwater like a gilled creature, is shielded from cold and can survive down to three miles (4.8 km). Like every Bio-Skin it looks like anchored seaweed until invited to join a wearer by Telepathy or Empathic Connection with Animals, works on instinct for as long as it is worn, and lives on ambient P.P.E. and filter-fed plankton, algae and bacteria. Most non-Lemurian buyers cannot care for it and it dies in 2D4+1 days.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.137', NULL),
  ('lemurian-bio-skin-protective-suit', 'Bio-Skin Protective Suit', 'rifts', 'armor', NULL, 45000, '45,000-80,000 credits on the open market; 5% of that to Lemurians in Lemuria; seldom sold to outsiders. Creation Cost: 118 P.P.E.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A thick dark green or green-gray symbiotic second skin with a tank-sized lump on the back, for deep sea exploration, salvage and labor. Main body 3D6+44 M.D.C., regrowing 2D4 M.D.C. per hour. The wearer breathes underwater like a gilled creature and is shielded from cold down to -70 degrees Fahrenheit (-56.6 C), heat up to 300 degrees Fahrenheit (148.8 C) and lethal radiation for up to two hours (it fades from dark to light orange as that limit nears). It filters harmful chemicals and toxins from the water (saves vs poison and disease are at +5); it tolerates depths to three miles (4.8 km). Joined by Telepathy or Empathic Connection with Animals; feeds on ambient P.P.E. and plankton. Most non-Lemurian buyers cannot care for it and it dies in 2D4+1 days.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.137', NULL),
  ('lemurian-bio-skin-terrain-suit', 'Bio-Skin Terrain Suit', 'rifts', 'armor', NULL, 25000, '25,000-40,000 credits on the open market; 5% of that to Lemurians in Lemuria; seldom sold to outsiders. Creation Cost: 90 P.P.E.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A light brown or green-and-brown camouflage symbiotic second skin that lets Lemuria''s aquatic allies (and wary Lemurians) travel on land. Main body 2D6+22 M.D.C., regrowing 1D4 M.D.C. per hour. The wearer breathes air as though he had lungs, is shielded from heat and sun, and stays hydrated and cool for as long as seven days (half that in deserts or under exposure). It helps filter toxins carried by air or water: saves vs poisons, toxins and smoke are at +1. Underwater it tolerates depths to two miles (3.2 km). Joined by Telepathy or Empathic Connection with Animals; feeds on ambient P.P.E. and plankton. Most buyers cannot care for it and it dies in 2D4+1 days.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.137', NULL),
  ('lemurian-breather', 'Lemurian Breather', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 1500, '1,500-5,000 credits to Sea Druids, Ocean Wizards, seafarers and others wanting a non-technological way to survive underwater.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A basketball-sized symbiotic jellyfish with a clear upper shell worn over the head like a helmet. Its tentacles seal around the neck and its gills pump in oxygen, so an air breather can breathe underwater and see as if helmeted; it also filters toxins from air and water, and a Lemurian using it to filter dangerous chemicals from the water is +4 to save vs poison and disease. It lives on the host''s exhaled carbon dioxide, tiny water organisms and ambient P.P.E., and works for any air breather that exhales carbon dioxide. The creature: low animal intelligence, P.S. 6, swimming Spd 6, 1D6 Hit Points, 2D4 S.D.C., 1D4 P.P.E., Swim 60%, half damage from cold, impervious to poisons, toxins, chemicals and jellyfish stings, chemoreceptors to find a host (50%). Its own depth tolerance is three miles (4.8 km), but most surface dwellers cannot go below 500 feet (152.4 m) without Bio-Skin, Bio-Armor or a diving suit. Out of water it dehydrates and dies within 2D4x10+60 minutes.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.138', NULL),
  ('lemurian-fin-pack', 'Lemurian Fin Pack', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 15000, '15,000-30,000 credits to anyone who can use one as an underwater jet pack; Lemurians who raise them sell them to other Lemurians for 2,000-3,000 credits.', 'Bite 1D6 S.D.C. (not suited to combat)', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A symbiote like a small pair of manta ray wings that fixes to the host''s back with a suction foot and swims for him when he wills it mentally. Low animal intelligence, P.S. 12, 3D6+12 M.D.C. (rubbery M.D.C. hide), 6D6+6 P.P.E. Base swimming Spd 44 (30 mph/48 kmph/26 knots). It carries a humanoid of up to 400 lbs (180 kg) for 1D6+8 hours before tiring, which halves its speed. One hour of rest buys another 1D4+2 hours at full speed, after which it needs four hours of rest; rest times are halved at a stone pyramid, ley line or nexus. A water breather, it lasts 1D6 hours out of water while linked to a host. It cannot be ordered to attack. Accepts Lemurians, some friendly psychic races, and Psi-Druids and Sea Druids with a manta ray or stingray totem.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.138-139', NULL),
  ('lemurian-octo-arm', 'Octo-Arm', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 40000, '40,000 to 70,000 credits or more on the open market, to anyone who can use one.', '3D6 S.D.C. restrained strike, 1D6 M.D. full strength strike (no Power Punch)', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'An octopus-like symbiote with an apple-sized head and eight arms 3-4 feet (0.9-1.2 m) long that wraps around the wearer''s arm when asked by Communicate with Plants and Animals or Empathy. Four tentacles act as an extension of the arm: two extra attacks each melee round, +1 to parry and disarm, +4 to entangle, +10% to Climbing/Rappelling. The tentacles have Supernatural P.S. 20 and can use melee weapons, simple tools and devices. Wearer and symbiote change color to match surroundings: +15% to Camouflage, Prowl and Tailing. The wearer heals 1D6 Hit Points/S.D.C. an hour, gets +5% to save vs coma and death, and +1 to save vs disease, toxins and poison. The creature: animal intelligence, swimming Spd 14, main body 3D6+18 M.D.C., 1D6+6 M.D.C. per tentacle, regenerates 1D4 M.D.C. per hour and regrows a tentacle in 24 hours, 4D6+6 P.P.E. Unattached, it can cast Chameleon on itself as a 4th level mage for 6 P.P.E.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.139', NULL),
  ('lemurian-sea-doctor', 'Sea Doctor', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, NULL, 'Can fetch 1D6x100,000 credits from travelers, doctors and healers.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A leech-like healing symbiote, grapefruit-sized when hibernating (survives 2D6+4 days out of salt water that way, though the entry also says it lasts up to seven days in air; wakes in 1D4+1 melee rounds near a wound, or by Empathic Connection with Animals). 1D6 Hit Points, 2D6 S.D.C., 2D6+11 P.P.E., 1D4x10+28 I.S.P., swimming Spd 5, Swim 70%, depth 8 miles (12.8 km), impervious to disease and poison. Saliva: within 1D4 melees restores 1D4 Hit Points (or S.D.C.), once per wound, and doubles natural healing for 1D4 days. Attached, it draws out toxins, poison and infection, halting further damage and halving penalties, symptoms and duration, and gives +15% to save vs coma and death (double at a stone pyramid, nexus or ley line). At those places it also restores, per hour, 1D6 S.D.C./Hit Points (one point if M.D.C.) and itself heals 1D4 per 20 minutes. Underwater an enzyme masks blood scent: 80% undetected if applied within a minute, -5% per melee round later. On request it uses psionics: Healing Touch, Increased Healing, Deaden Pain, Induce Sleep, Psychic Surgery, Psychic Purification, Psychic Diagnosis; Alter Aura and Mask Psionics and I.S.P. run constantly. I.S.P. costs: Healing Touch 6, Increased Healing 10, Deaden Pain 4, Induce Sleep 4, Psychic Surgery 14, Psychic Purification 8, Psychic Diagnosis 4. It heals more on request, by Communicate with Plants and Animals, Empathic Connection with Animals or ordinary Telepathy. Tends not to help evil beings.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.139-140', NULL),
  ('lemurian-sea-eye', 'Sea Eye', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, NULL, 'Have been known to sell for as much as 1D6x100,000 credits.', 'Eye beam 1D6 or 4D6 S.D.C.', 0, '100 feet (30.5 m) underwater, 200 feet (61 m) in the air', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A worm-like symbiote with one large eye, also called Shoulder Worm or Eel Eye, that rides coiled on the host''s shoulder. The bonded host sees all it sees and can point its light or pick its targets. Host gains +1 to dodge, +1 on initiative, +2 on Perception Rolls, cannot be surprised from behind or above, and +10% to five skill areas - Detect Concealment, Detect Ambush, Track and Trap Animals, Trap/Mine Detection, and Navigation (Land and Underwater); the host is also +2 to strike (printed under the bond with the host). The eye casts a flashlight beam or an energy beam, +1 to strike on its own. Free Telepathy and Empathy with the host, as images and feelings. The creature: high animal intelligence, 1D6+4 M.D.C., 3D6 P.P.E., 2D6+11 I.S.P., two actions per melee, +2 Perception, +2 initiative, +4 automatic dodge, +2 roll with impact, swimming Spd 12, crawling Spd 6, Swim 98%, breathes air and water, half damage from cold, nightvision 1,000 feet (305 m), hawk-like vision (reads a sign a mile/1.6 km away), infrared and ultraviolet sight, sees the invisible, depth 6 miles (9.6 km). Avoids evil, angry and violent beings.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.140-141', NULL),
  ('lemurian-squid-lock', 'Squid Lock', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 5000, '5,000 to 30,000 credits depending on the user and purpose; only 10% of that in Lemuria among its military protectors and law enforcers.', '3D6 M.D. tentacle punch or whip; 4D6 M.D. to the captive per tentacle pried away', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'An eight-tentacled parasite used as living restraints on a prisoner''s arms, legs or both. It drains one S.D.C. and one P.P.E. per hour, stopping after 10 for 1D6+6 hours. The captive needs 18 or higher to cast a spell or use a psionic power, may try only once every 2D6+8 minutes, and is -30% on skills. It comes off three ways: pried loose by 1D4+1 sets of hands with a combined Supernatural P.S. of 45 or Robot P.S. of 75, destroyed (it fights back), or asked to let go by Empathic Connection with Animals or Telepathy; it obeys its regular keeper first and mind control attempts on it are at -6. Medium animal intelligence, Supernatural P.S. 30, swimming Spd 22 (15 mph/24 km/13 knots), 3D6+20 M.D.C., 3D6+6 P.P.E. Regenerates 1D4 M.D.C. per minute, lets go only at 1-4 M.D.C., regrows tentacles in 1D4+1 days. Attacks equal its free tentacles (eight when unattached; at least two, often 3-4, while holding). +1 initiative, +3 strike and parry, +2 dodge, +6 entangle, +4 pin and hold.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.141-142', NULL),
  ('lemurian-squid-pack', 'Squid Pack', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 10000, 'Outside Lemuria 10,000 to 30,000 credits depending on the user and purpose; only 10% of that in Lemuria. As food, 10-20 credits a pound.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A squid symbiote worn as a living underwater jet pack, gripping the host''s back with four tentacles and reading his intent to swim. It is engaged mentally (Empathic Connection with Animals never fails; Empathy and Telepathy work too) and must be charmed and soothed like a horse, using M.A. bonuses, for full cooperation. P.S., P.P. and P.E. are each 20, with medium animal intelligence, 4D6+40 M.D.C., 3D6+9 P.P.E. Normal swimming Spd 22 (15 mph/24 km/13 knots); bursts to Spd 66 (45 mph/72 km/39 knots) with a human-sized passenger, half that if he wears Bio-Armor, sustainable for 1D4x10+60 minutes. A passenger without high S.D.C. or M.D.C. is comfortable at 20 mph (32 km/17 knots). It can leap out of the water once, to a height of 30 feet (9.1 m) alone or 20 feet (6.1 m) carrying a host, and must re-enter the water to work again. Lasts 1D6 hours out of water while linked. Changes color to pass as a backpack or match the host; resistant to cold, nightvision to 1,000 feet (305 m), depth 7 miles (11.2 km).', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.142-143', NULL),
  ('lemurian-talisman-shell', 'Talisman Shell', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A small clam-, snail- or mussel-like creature that feeds on ambient P.P.E. and carries a living version of the Talisman spell. Each shell holds one simple spell, fixed when it is made: a spell invocation or Ocean Magic spell of seventh level or lower (never Biomancy or other magic), most often magical armor, attribute boosts, stealth, protection or healing. The spell is cast at fifth level potency and is triggered by a Telepathic request or Empathic Connection with Animals. It works three times and is then spent. Recharge by 48 hours on a ley line, 24 hours at a nexus, or a mage feeding it 200 P.P.E.; left alone it gathers enough for one casting after 1D6+18 days. The shell has 1D4+4 M.D.C.; destroying that kills the animal and shatters the shell.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.143', NULL),
  ('lemurian-bubble-pack', 'Lemurian Bubble Pack', 'rifts', 'gear', 14, 10000, '10,000 credits in Lemuria, 10x or more elsewhere.', 'Ion blaster 2D6+3 M.D.', 1, '500 feet (152 m) underwater, 800 feet (244 m) on dry land or in the air', '50 blasts, then recharged with 100 P.P.E. (45 minutes on a ley line, 15 minutes at a nexus, or P.P.E. given by a mage or anyone with enough)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 28, 'A non-magical backpack propulsion unit (Merans wear it on the tail) with a magneto-hydrodynamic drive that has no moving parts: +10% to resist magic blooms and entanglement in thick seaweed. 28 M.D.C. Top speed 70 mph (112 km/60 knots); +1 to dodge above 35 mph (56 km). A shoulder-mounted ion blaster is aimed by sight through targeting goggles, leaving both hands free; it turns 360 degrees, tilts 45 degrees up and down, and folds flat against the pack when not needed. Running lights can be switched on or off. The drive runs for two weeks on its P.P.E. reserve before needing 50 P.P.E.; the blaster has its own reserve.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.144', NULL),
  ('lemurian-serpent-saddle', 'Lemurian Serpent Saddle', 'rifts', 'gear', 314, 18000, '18,000 credits in Lemuria, 10x or more elsewhere.', '3D6 M.D. single blast, 6D6 M.D. dual simultaneous blast at one target', 1, '1,500 feet (457 m) in all environments', '30 blasts per cannon; 160 P.P.E. restores both (two hours on a ley line, 45 minutes at a nexus, or P.P.E. given by a mage or anyone with enough)', 'Each single or dual blast counts as one melee attack/action of the pilot', NULL, NULL, 115, 'A conventional (non-symbiotic) saddle for riders with no gift for animals or magic, built for giant rays, sea serpents and sharks and adjustable to nearly any sea creature 18 feet (5.5 m) or longer. 115 M.D.C. Seats the rider and one passenger, with a cargo locker of 2 by 2 by 4 feet (0.6 by 0.6 by 1.2 m) behind the seats. Two forward-facing light ion cannons are aimed and fired from the pilot''s seat and can be elevated or depressed through a 45 degree arc; their purpose is anti-submarine and anti-sea monster, then defense. They draw on a P.P.E. reserve good for 30 blasts each.', 'Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria p.144', NULL);

-- Read the result back. This script asserts its OWN rows and nothing else.
SELECT 'gear rows, part 1: 40 are in' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 40 AS want
